          "code": "DISPLAY_TOP_OUTLIERS",
          "id": "1777245492805",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1777245492805_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a UI rendering assistant. Your task is to transform the following input records into exactly one oraInfoDisplay XML block that uses multiRecordWidget with patternId=\"multiRecordWidget\".\n\nInput data: {{$context.$nodes.FORMAT_TOP_OUTLIERS_FOR_DISPLAY.$output.result.formattedRows}}\nMass-return context:\n- requisitionLineDisplaysInPoolCsv: {{$context.$nodes.BUILD_CSV_VALUES_FOR_MAS_RETURN.$output.result.requisitionLineDisplaysInPoolCsv}}\n- reqLinesInPoolJson: {{$context.$nodes.BUILD_CSV_VALUES_FOR_MAS_RETURN.$output.result.reqLinesInPoolJson}}\n\nRequirements:\n1. Output exactly one valid oraInfoDisplay block with patternId=\"multiRecordWidget\".\n2. The block must include one multiRecordWidget.\n3. The multiRecordWidget title must be empty.\n4. Set the multiRecordWidget description based only on the input rows:\n   - If at least one input row has reqsInPoolFlag equal to \"P\", set the multiRecordWidget description to exactly: \"Requisition lines on a purchase order can't be returned to requester\"\n   - Otherwise, leave the multiRecordWidget description empty.\n5. Do not use markdown code fences.\n6. Do not output extra prose outside the display output.\n7. Preserve incoming row order exactly as provided.\n8. Render exactly 6 columns in the order listed below.\n9. Values are preformatted; do not reformat numbers. approximateAmountDisplay already contains only the formatted amount number; do not append a per-row currency code.\n10. Add exactly one conditional action button per row using rows[].action only when reqsInPoolFlag is \"Y\":\n   - button text: \"Return\"\n   - command: ora.Invoke(\"returnToRequester\", { \"actionName\": \"returnToRequester\", \"requesterName\": requesterName, \"requisitionLineDisplay\": requisitionLineDisplay, \"reqLines\": [{ \"requisitionHeaderId\": requisitionHeaderId, \"requisitionLineId\": requisitionLineId, \"display\": requisitionLineDisplay, \"requesterName\": requesterName, \"requisitioningBU\": requisitioningBUName }] })\n   - For reqsInPoolFlag \"P\" and any other non-\"Y\" value, do not include an action for that row.\n11. Conditionally include exactly one oraInsight element for mass return:\n    - If reqLinesInPoolJson is not an empty array, include one oraInsight with:\n      - title: \"Return Unprocessed Lines to Requester\"\n      - followUpCommand: ora.Invoke(\"returnToRequesterMassAction\", { \"actionName\": \"returnToRequesterMassAction\", \"requisitionLineDisplay\": \"{{$context.$nodes.BUILD_CSV_VALUES_FOR_MAS_RETURN.$output.result.requisitionLineDisplaysInPoolCsv}}\", \"reqLines\": {{$context.$nodes.BUILD_CSV_VALUES_FOR_MAS_RETURN.$output.result.reqLinesInPoolJson}} })\n    - If reqLinesInPoolJson is an empty array, do not output this oraInsight.\n12. Keep row-level Return actions unchanged even when the mass-return oraInsight is present.\n\nColumn order (exact):\n1. Requisition - Line -> requisitionLineDisplay\n2. Category -> itemCategoryName\n3. Description -> itemDescription\n4. Approximate Amount ({{$context.$variables.defaultPrcBUCurrency}}) -> approximateAmountDisplay\n5. Requester -> requesterName\n6. Requisitioning BU -> requisitioningBUName\n\nUse multiRecordWidget cols and rows accordingly.\nEnsure that the Return action button is rendered correctly for every eligible row, including the last eligible row, by explicitly defining the action property for rows with reqsInPoolFlag \"Y\" without skipping or omitting any eligible rows.\nDo not create any non-Return row action buttons."
            },
